  into  and stuff that we never use and so my  takeaway  was that there's so much that we have  that we don't actually  need and so that was a that was a big  moment and your  overhead used to be sixteen hundred  dollars and went down to  two hundred dollars yeah my rent  alone was sixteen hundred dollars before  i moved into my tiny  and that didn't even include utilities  so now  my space rent for my house plus my  utilities plus  everything is yeah less than a few  hundred bucks a month okay  and then also why did you decide to  create this village  which if women are dealing with divorce  and want to downsize and find a  community  what was that impetus for you  to get that started because you did this  for yourself but you're really doing it  for other people as well  yeah i mean i tiny house living changed  my life  so dramatically so the number one thing  that i set out to do with the tiny house  village was really to inspire other  people  to step outside their comfort zone to  try on tiny for a weekend  and see what it feels like um some of my  guests  come and they go and they actually build  a tiny house for themselves  some of them are like no way not for me  but you don't know until you try  well i think you're right and now i know  these tiny houses can have some design  challenges is that true oh my god  tiny houses huge design challenge  so you have to design them intentionally  not by the square foot but by the square  inch and not just design challenges but  also  placement challenges  i think people should think that way no  matter what  [Music]  you
 

